  "prediction": "Answer_9:\nCarver is 5 years less than twice the age of his son.\nLet's call the son's age x.\nThen Carver's age is 2x - 5.\nWe are told that Carver is 45.\nSo 2x - 5 = 45.\n2x = 50.\nx = 25.\nThe answer is 25.\n\nAnswer_10:\nThe train goes 75 miles from the first city to the second city.\n100 miles from the second city to the third city.\n75 + 100 = 175 miles.\nThe train goes 50 miles less than that combined distance to go from the third city to the first city.\nSo it goes 175 - 50 = 125 miles.\nThe total distance is 75 + 100 + 125 = 300 miles.\nThe train goes 300 miles 3 times a day.\n300 * 3 = 900 miles per day.\nThe train needs service every 18,000 miles.\nSo it will need service after 18,000 / 900 = 20 days.\nThe answer is 20.\n\nAnswer_11:\nA bed for a Rottweiler takes 8 pounds of stuffing.\nA bed for a chihuahua takes 2 pounds of stuffing.\nA bed for a collie takes the average amount of stuffing between the first two kinds of beds.\nThe average of 8 and 2 is (8 + 2) / 2 = 10.\nSo a bed for a collie takes 10 pounds of stuffing.\nMark needs to make 4 chihuahua beds and 3 collie beds.\n4 * 2 = 8 pounds of stuffing for the chihuahua beds.\n3 * 10 = 30 pounds of stuffing for the collie beds.\n8 + 30 = 38.\nThe answer is 38.\n\nAnswer_12:\nJohn drives 200 miles at 70 mph.\n200 / 70 = 2.86 hours.\nHe had to take a detour that added 10 miles to his trip.\nSo he drove 200 + 10 = 210 miles.\n210 / 70 = 3 hours.\nHe drove 240 miles at 80 mph.\n240 / 80 = 3 hours.\nThe total time is 2.86 + 3 + 3 = 8.86 hours.\nThe answer is 8.86.\n\nAnswer_13:\nThere are 96 fourth-graders.\n43 of them are girls.\nSo there are 96 - 43 = 53 boys.\nOn Friday, 5 fourth-grade girls and 4 fourth-grade boys were absent.\nSo there are 43 - 5 = 38 girls.\nThere are 53 - 4 = 49 boys.\nThe answer is 49.\n\nAnswer_14:\nThere are 6 girls in the park.\nIf there are twice the number of boys in the park, then there are 6 * 2 = 12 boys.\n6 + 12 = 18.\nThe answer is 18.\n\nAnswer_15:\nJane scored 15 points on her first test.\nShe scored 18 points on her second test.\nSo she scored 15 + 18 = 33 points.\nShe needs to score at least 42 points.\nSo she needs to score 42 - 33 = 9 points.\nThe answer is 9.\n\nAnswer_16:\n3 customers were kicked out for refusing to wear masks.\nA number equals to four times that many minus 5 were kicked out for shoplifting.\nSo 4 * 3 - 5 = 7.\nThree times the number of shoplifters were kicked out for physical violence over goods on sale.\nSo 3 * 7 = 21.\nA total of 50 people were kicked out of the Walmart.\nSo 3 + 7 + 21 = 31 people were kicked out for other reasons.\nThe answer is 31.\n\nAnswer_17:\nErin has 3 times more points than Sara.\nSara scored 8 points.\nSo Erin scored 3 * 8 = 24 points.\nErin scored 14 points.\nSo she had 14 - 24 = -10 points before.\nThe answer is -10.\n\nAnswer_18:\n44 seniors need to receive awards.\nEach senior receives a picture frame that costs $20.\nSo 44 * 20 = $880.\nEach picture frame needs to be etched with the logo for an additional 20% cost per frame.\nSo 20% of 20 is 4.\nSo each picture frame costs 20 + 4 = 24 dollars.\nSo 44 * 24 = $1056.\n2 of the seniors will also receive pins that are $5.\nSo 2 * 5 = $10.\n1/4 of the seniors are officers and they will need to receive cords that are $12 each.\nSo 1/4 of 44 is 11.\nSo 11 * 12 = $132.\nSo the total cost is 1056 + 10 + 132 = $1198.\nThe answer is 1198.\n\nAnswer_19:\nA hand-painted wallpaper costs $400 at the market.\nA DIY will saves 20% after considering the materials cost.\nSo 20% of 400 is 80.\nSo the DIY costs 400 - 80 = $320.\nThe answer is 320.\n\nAnswer_20:\nA shoe store sold 14 pairs of tennis shoes on Friday.\nEach pair has 2 shoes.\nSo 14 * 2 = 28 shoes.\nThey sold double that number of shoes on Saturday.\nSo 28 * 2 = 56 shoes.\nThey sold one-half the amount that they did the day before on Sunday.\nSo 56 / 2 = 28 shoes.\nSix people returned their pairs because they didn't fit.\nSo 28 - 6 = 22 shoes.\nThe total number of shoes sold is 28 + 56 + 28 = 112 shoes.\nThe answer is 112.\n\nAnswer_21:\nHallie had dance practice for 1 hour on Tuesdays.\nShe had dance practice for 2 hours on Thursdays.\nShe had dance practice for twice as long as Tuesday's night class on Saturdays.\nSo 2 * 1 = 2 hours.\nShe had dance practice for 1 + 2 + 2 = 5 hours.\nThe answer is 5.\n\nAnswer_22:\nA company bought $400000 worth of equipment.\n40% of the total number were faulty.\nSo 40% of 400000 is 160000.\nThe total amount of money spent on functioning pieces of equipment is 400000 - 160000 = $240000.\nThe answer is 240000.\n\nAnswer_23:\nMary has 30 sheep.\nShe gets 1 kg of milk from half of them.\nSo 30 / 2 = 15 sheep.\nShe gets 2 kg of milk from the other half.\nSo 30 / 2 = 15 sheep.\nShe gets 1 + 2 = 3 kg of milk from each sheep.\nSo she gets 3 * 15 = 45 kg of milk from half of the sheep.\nShe gets 3 * 15 = 45 kg of milk from the other half.\nSo she gets 45 + 45 = 90 kg of milk every day.\nThe answer is 90.\n\nAnswer_24:\nMrs. Sherman made a dozen bread rolls.\nShe fed 6 children with one each.\nSo 6 children ate 6 rolls.\nShe broke each of the remaining rolls into 8 pieces.\nSo 12 - 6 = 6 rolls.\nShe fed them to the chickens.\nSo 6 * 8 = 48 pieces.\nThe answer is 48.\n\nAnswer_25:\nThere are 40 pupils in a class.\nHalf of the class likes blue.\nSo 40 / 2 = 20 pupils.\nOne-fourth of the remaining likes green.\nSo 40 - 20 = 20 pupils.\n20 / 4 = 5 pupils.\nThe rest likes yellow.\nSo 20 - 5 = 15 pupils.\nThe answer is 15.\n\nAnswer_26:\nLucy sold all the apples picked on Monday.\nShe got $56 from selling the apples picked on Monday.\nShe sold 56 / 4 = 14 apples.\nShe picked 12 apples on Tuesday.\nShe picked double the number of apples she did the previous day on Wednesday.\nSo 2 * 12 = 24 apples.\nShe picked 14 + 12 + 24 = 50 apples.\nThe answer is 50.\n\nAnswer_27:\nLindsay washed 10 pairs of socks and 15 loose socks.\nEach pair has 2 socks.\nSo 10 * 2 = 20 socks.\nShe washed 20 + 15 = 35 socks.\nThere a